#: ../../tools/ensembl_vep_tools.rst:66 77c0baad9b6d4c25a1e9ba1467396b7e
msgid ""
"**Description**: Predict functional consequences of a genetic variant "
"using its dbSNP rs identifier via the Ensembl Variant Effect Predictor "
"(VEP). Returns impact on genes, transcripts, and proteins including "
"SIFT/PolyPhen scores, consequence types, amino acid changes, and "
"colocated variants. Useful when you have a variant's rs number from GWAS,"
" clinical reports, or literature. Example: 'rs7903146' (TCF7L2 T2D "
"variant), 'rs429358' (APOE Alzheimer variant)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_vep_tools.rst:70 92960252f0734b51b53e765522c93e49
msgid ""
"``variant_id`` (string) (optional) dbSNP rs identifier. Examples: "
"'rs7903146' (TCF7L2, type 2 diabetes), 'rs429358' (APOE, Alzheimer's), "
"'rs1801133' (MTHFR C677T). Aliases: rsid, rs\\_id."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_vep_tools.rst:73 e35d9b3f21d440a6ac76bde792ffe206
msgid ""
"``rsid`` (string) (optional) Alias for variant\\_id. dbSNP rs identifier "
"(e.g., 'rs7903146')."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ensembl_vep_tools.rst:76 df36dc7e14cd456da374fb8b33f2a70d
msgid ""
"``rs_id`` (string) (optional) Alias for variant\\_id. dbSNP rs identifier"
" (e.g., 'rs7903146')."
msgstr ""

